  "A Google DeepMind-affiliated team led by Nahema Marchal argues that as large language models increasingly curate information and dispense personalized advice, poorly designed \"epistemic agents\" risk cognitive deskilling and societal epistemic drift — and proposes a three-part framework of trustworthy competence, alignment with human knowledge goals, and institutional safeguards like provenance tracking to keep AI-mediated knowledge reliable.": "Gulu logwirizana ndi Google DeepMind, lotsogozedwa ndi Nahema Marchal, likunena kuti pamene ma large language model akungowonjezera kusankha zidziwitso ndi kupereka malangizo a munthu payekha, \"ma-ejenti a chidziwitso\" opangidwa mosasamala ali pachiwopsezo chochepetsa luso laumunthu ndi kusochera kwa chidziwitso mu gulu la anthu — ndipo akupereka njira yokhala ndi magawo atatu: luso lodalirika, kugwirizana ndi zolinga za chidziwitso cha anthu, ndi zitetezo za mabungwe monga kutsatira gwero, kuti chidziwitso chochokera mu AI chikhalebe chodalirika.",
