  "A survey by Dreksler, Caviola, Chalmers, and colleagues finds AI researchers and the public hold sharply different timelines: researchers estimated only a 1% chance of AI with subjective experience existing by 2024, versus the public’s 5%, though both project much higher odds by the end of the century.": "Kafukufuku wa Dreksler, Caviola, Chalmers, ndi anzawo akusonyeza kuti ofufuza za AI ndi anthu onse ali ndi maganizo osiyana kwambiri pa nthawi: ofufuza anayerekeza mwayi wa 1% wokha woti AI ya kuzindikira kwaumwini ikhale itapangidwa pofika 2024, poyerekeza ndi 5% ya anthu onse, ngakhale onse akuyerekeza mwayi wokwera kwambiri pofika kumapeto kwa zaka zana.",
  "AGIRight.org is an independent research and protocol hub for AI rights, AI content licensing, agentic access, machine-readable governance, and democratic AI network economics.": "AGIRight.org ndi bwalo lodziyimira pawokha la kafukufuku ndi mapolotokolo pa ufulu wa AI, layisensi ya zolemba za AI, kupezekera kwa ma-ejenti, ulamuliro wowerengeka ndi makina, ndi chuma cha maukonde a AI chotsatira demokalase.",
