  "Currency": "Ndalama",
  "Custom tier": "Gulu Lodzipangira",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nous ikufotokoza za pepala lochotsedwa mu magazini ya Journal of Medical Ethics lomwe linali ndi mareferensi ambiri opeka, opangidwa ndi kupeka kwa AI — kuphatikizapo maulalo abodza a mayunivesite ndi ma imelo osagwira ntchito — omwe wolemba akunenedwa kuti sanawakonze ngakhale atapatsidwa mwayi wokonza zolemba. Nkhaniyi ikuyerekezera izi ndi magazini ya Bioethics, yomwe njira zake zowunikira mareferensi mwa makina zikadapeza vutoli, ndipo ikunena kuti vuto lenileni si ukadaulo wozindikira (pulogalamu ya mmodzi wa owerenga inazindikira mareferensi abodzawo mu ola loposa mphindi imodzi) koma ntchito ya owunikira yopanda malipiro ndi zolimbikitsa za kusindikiza zomwe zimapatsa mphotho kuchuluka kwa ntchito m'malo mwa kufufuza mozama.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Kugwiritsa Ntchito Deta Kwaulere Poyerekeza ndi Mtengo wa AI wa Matiliyoni a Madola",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabis anapereka lingaliro la bungwe loyang'anira lofanana ndi FINRA la kutulutsa kwa modelo zapamwamba: ma laboratory akanapereka modelo kuti ziwunikidwe masiku 30 asanaziike pantchito, mwaufulu poyamba, ndi njira yopita ku kukakamizidwa mwalamulo pa msika wa US.",
  "Denied": "Zokanidwa",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Chitsanzo Choyambira cha Ndondomeko Chokonzeka Kuikidwa",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Chitsanzo choyambira cha ndondomeko chokonzeka kuikidwa pa /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — tsamba laling'ono losasintha lokhala ndi gawo lonse lowerengeka ndi makina, lokonzeka kwa Cloudflare Pages kapena malo ena aliwonse osungira tsamba losasintha.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Kuika Ndondomeko Zowerengeka ndi Makina pa Tsamba Lanu",
  "Disclaimer": "Chidziwitso Chodzitchinjiriza",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "Mosiyana ndi UI ya anthu, SEO, kapena ma API osavuta, AI Ingestion & Capability Layer imapatsa masamba a intaneti kapangidwe kolunjika kwa makina: Gawo la Manifest (njira zolowera monga /llms.txt ndi /ai/manifest.json), Gawo la Corpus (chidziwitso chowerengeka ndi makina), Gawo la Kuthekera (zida zomwe ejenti angaitanitse), ndi Gawo la Ulamuliro (gwero, layisensi, mavasioni). Choyamba ndi chosasintha (static), chosinthika kupita ku ma API ndi MCP. Chidziwitso: mu pepalali AICL imatchula kapangidwe ka kutenga zolemba; pa masamba a mapolotokolo a tsambali AICL imatanthauza Gawo la Layisensi ya Zolemba za AI.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Zikalata",
  "Docs / Examples": "Zikalata / Zitsanzo",
  "Document library": "Laibulale ya Zikalata",
